From b95385cb37338f72884f3741d2edddd40f2a857b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan Miesch <bpmiesch@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:03:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix tls_set() default when ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 is missing

When tls_version is None, tls_set() read ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 before
checking for PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT. CPython built against OpenSSL >= 4.0
no longer defines the version-specific PROTOCOL_TLSv1* constants
(python/cpython#146207), so tls_set() raised AttributeError even though
the value was about to be replaced.

Only read PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 when it exists. The PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT and
PROTOCOL_TLS fallbacks are kept, so behavior is unchanged on existing
runtimes.

Add tests that tls_set() defaults to PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT, including
when ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 is not defined.

Assisted-by: Anthropic Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Signed-off-by: Brendan Miesch <bpmiesch@gmail.com>

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/eclipse-paho/paho.mqtt.python/commit/b95385cb37338f72884f3741d2edddd40f2a857b]
---
 src/paho/mqtt/client.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/paho/mqtt/client.py b/src/paho/mqtt/client.py
index 3f7c3d125..df36c9cf1 100644
--- a/src/paho/mqtt/client.py
+++ b/src/paho/mqtt/client.py
@@ -1283,7 +1283,8 @@ def tls_set(
 
         # Create SSLContext object
         if tls_version is None:
-            tls_version = ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2
+            if hasattr(ssl, "PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2"):
+                tls_version = ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2
             # If the python version supports it, use highest TLS version automatically
             if hasattr(ssl, "PROTOCOL_TLS_CLIENT"):
                 # This also enables CERT_REQUIRED and check_hostname by default.
